# Environment configuration for JoustMania
# Copy this file to the git-ignored .env.local (never over the tracked .env,
# which holds the release IMAGE_TAG) and keep it private; ./setup.sh offers this:
#   install -m 600 .env.example .env.local
# Never set IMAGE_TAG in .env.local on the Pi: the pinned checkout decides it
# (UC-060 BR-003).

# ---- Decision-backend API keys (#1244) ----
# Do NOT put API keys in .env: it is TRACKED in git despite .gitignore.
# Export them in your shell, or put them in the git-ignored .env.local and load
# both files (later wins; passing --env-file disables the implicit .env):
#   docker compose --env-file .env --env-file .env.local up -d
# The keys go straight to the agent (no gateway); an empty key keeps that
# backend unavailable, so decisions fall back to rules. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY also
# serves the post-game retro / experiment proposer when
# the inference.backend flag is claude (#1234, #1810).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# JEV_API_KEY=

# ---- Dashboard host names (UC-005 BR-003, #1450) ----
# Extra host names the operator uses to open the dashboard (comma-separated).
# Always allowed without this: IP literals, localhost, and the Pi's own host
# name and <hostname>.local (compose mounts the host's /etc/hostname). The
# unpair endpoint answers 403 for any other Host (DNS-rebinding guard).
# Default: empty.
# JOUSTMANIA_HOSTNAMES=joustmania.example,stage-pi

# ---- Telemetry environment (#2646) ----
# Value of the OTel resource attribute deployment.environment on every service,
# flagd and the collector. Backends (gateway export, #2571) filter on it.
# Default: development (local and CI). The stage Pi sets production here:
# DEPLOYMENT_ENVIRONMENT=production

# ---- Opt-in compose profiles (UC-060) ----
# Put these in the git-ignored .env.local on the Pi, never in .env.
# The operator pad (UC-015, #2050) starts only with its profile. Set the whole
# comma-separated list in one place (e.g. operator-pad): a unit
# drop-in Environment=COMPOSE_PROFILES=... wins over .env.local, and a profile
# missing from the winning list is off (the start script removes its container).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=operator-pad
# GID of the host's input group (owner of /dev/input/event*), host identity
# (C-035, flags.md §15.2). `getent group input` shows it. Default: 996 (stage Pi).
# INPUT_GID=996
# Char major of the host's hidraw devices, for the pad's display (UC-016). Host
# identity (C-035, flags.md §15.2); scripts/setup/joustmania-compose.sh reads it
# from /proc/devices and wins over a different value here, so leave it unset on
# the Pi; it then adds docker-compose.operator-pad-hidraw.yml. Without a known
# major there is no hidraw rule (no display, the pad works).
# HIDRAW_MAJOR=240

# ---- Flagsmith link (UC-054, UC-055; services.md §7.3) ----
# Put these in the git-ignored .env.local, never in .env. Off by default: unless
# FLAGSMITH_LINK is exactly `on` the flag service never contacts Flagsmith (any
# value other than `on`/`off`, e.g. ON, true or 1, leaves the link off and is
# reported). With `on`, the four values below marked REQUIRED must be set
# (FLAGSMITH_PROJECT_ID a positive integer); if one is missing the service still
# starts with the link off. Either way GET /state names the bad variables (never
# their values) in config_error. The Flagsmith project needs edge identities,
# and the environment needs "Use identity overrides in local evaluation" on and
# no change requests; otherwise the link stays offline
# (identity_overrides_disabled, edge_required) or every push is refused. The
# link creates missing features and tags itself (FR-214); an existing name that
# differs only in case, or an archived feature, is refused.
# FLAGSMITH_LINK=on
# REQUIRED:
# FLAGSMITH_PROJECT_ID=12345
# REQUIRED, the client-side environment key (used in Admin API paths, not a secret):
# FLAGSMITH_ENVIRONMENT_KEY=
# REQUIRED secrets (C-016): server-side environment key (ser.…) for the
# environment document, and an organisation Admin API key for pushes (with
# RBAC, a role limited to the project):
# FLAGSMITH_SERVER_KEY=
# FLAGSMITH_ADMIN_API_KEY=
# Optional. Defaults: Flagsmith SaaS URLs, poll every 30 s (5..30, NFR-058),
# 5 pushes/s (1..50), 5 s timeout (1..60). An invalid or out-of-range value
# (e.g. FLAGSMITH_POLL_SECONDS=60, a relative URL) is ignored: its default is
# used, the link stays on, and config_error plus an error log name the variable.
# URLs are absolute http(s); the two API bases get a trailing / added.
# FLAGSMITH_REALTIME_URL (SSE, a paid Flagsmith feature, e.g.
# https://realtime.flagsmith.com/) only shortens the delay; empty = polling
# only. The health webhook URL (a Flagsmith "Webhook" feature-health provider)
# is a secret; empty = no health events.
# FLAGSMITH_API_URL=https://api.flagsmith.com/api/v1/
# FLAGSMITH_DOCUMENT_URL=https://edge.api.flagsmith.com/api/v1/
# FLAGSMITH_POLL_SECONDS=30
# FLAGSMITH_PUSH_RATE=5
# FLAGSMITH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=5
# FLAGSMITH_REALTIME_URL=
# FLAGSMITH_HEALTH_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---- Gateway export of the game telemetry (UC-035 A7, #2571) ----
# Only read by docker-compose.gateway.yml (opt-in, see DEVELOPMENT.md "Gateway
# export"). Both are required by that file. On the Pi the two variables are the
# switch (#2622): with both set in .env.local as plain NAME=value lines, the
# wrapper adds the overlay to every compose call, the autostart included.
# After changing them recreate the collector:
#   ./scripts/setup/joustmania-compose.sh up -d otel-collector
# Elsewhere name the file yourself; a bare `docker compose -f ... up` does not
# read .env.local.
# The host has no scheme (https is fixed; host:port for a port other than 443);
# a value with a scheme (http://...) makes every export fail, nothing is sent.
# The gateway must answer /v1/* without a redirect: the collector follows
# redirects and sends the token along. The token is a secret (C-016).
# ORANGECASE_GATEWAY_HOST=otlp.example.org
# ORANGECASE_GATEWAY_TOKEN=
